  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **High Time** (1 review): Reviewer rates this as one of the better versions of the song [3]\n- **Easy Wind** (1 review): Reviewer notes that freely available recordings of this song are hard to find [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1969-10-24.aud.unknown.seaweed.122194.flac1644** (recommended): audience recording; 8 songs; 46 min; rated 1.75/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: This copy is clearer and more complete than the older Archive copy, and is in stereo, which is rare for a 1969 audience tape [7]\n- **gd69-10-24.aud.jools.19527.sbeok.shnf**: audience recording; 6 songs; 37 min; rated 2.8/5 by 5 [2]. Said about its sound: Audience recording's sound quality is rough, with little top end, which may put off some listeners [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Jefferson Airplane, Sons Of Champlin and Hot Tuna were also on the bill that night [1]\n- Reviewer says the archives list this as the first time China Cat Sunflower was played into I Know You Rider [6]\n- Reviewer calls it an average show for the period: weaker than 10/25 but better than 10/26 [7]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1969-10-24.aud.unknown.seaweed.122194.flac1644**: taped by seaweed1010; source: Source: AUD > ? > Cassette, kindly provided by Seaweed1010. [1]. Also: This transfer improves on the earlier ID-19527 tape, with patches from that copy added to make it more complete [1]\n- **gd69-10-24.aud.jools.19527.sbeok.shnf**: source: Audience [2]",
